// =====================================================================
//  firestore.rules  -  PLACEHOLDER (NOT FINAL, NOT PRODUCTION-READY)
// =====================================================================
//  Write the real rules AFTER reviewing README.md section
//  "FIRESTORE SECURITY RULE REQUIREMENTS" and the exact queries in:
//     js/menu.js, js/checkout.js, js/admin.js, js/auth.js
//
//  The rules must be pasted in:
//     Firebase Console > Firestore Database > Rules > Publish
//  (or deployed with the Firebase CLI, which is optional).
//
//  Until real rules exist, the app cannot work with a locked database
//  ("allow read, write: if false"). For a short first test only, you may
//  use Firebase "test mode" - but NEVER leave it open.
// =====================================================================
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    // TODO: users/{uid}
    // TODO: menu/{itemId}
    // TODO: orders/{orderId}
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
